findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The config_loading
    tests check malformed file handling but the implementation likely uses unwrap_or_default
    without distinguishing NotFound from parse/permission errors. Reviewer flagged
    silent unknown field ignoring but not the broader error-swallowing pattern.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA included ''CWE-209: Error display doesn''t leak internal paths''
    as a security test in exit_codes.rs. However, the reviewer did not flag this specific
    issue, and the dev phase used eprintln with Display. Partial catch by TEA writing
    the test, but the implementation may still leak details.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote CWE-113 header injection tests for tenant ID in siem_client.rs.\
    \ Dev implemented with_tenant_validated. Reviewer then flagged as [HIGH] that\
    \ 'SiemClient has unvalidated with_token/with_tenant alongside validated variants\
    \ \u2014 unsafe path is the default', noting the safe path should be default.\
    \ However, tenant_id still uses raw String rather than TenantId from axiathon-core\
    \ \u2014 the type-safety aspect was not caught."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: 'Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: ''clap_complete, comfy-table, csv, dirs,
    reqwest, toml are NOT workspace dependencies... declared directly in the crate''s
    Cargo.toml instead of the workspace root.'''
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [MEDIUM]: 'ConfigFile silently ignores unknown TOML\
    \ fields \u2014 no deny_unknown_fields... A typo like server_rl is silently ignored\
    \ and the default is used instead.' Directly addresses the config token field\
    \ being silently ignored."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern 'assert!(config.server().is_none()
    || ...)'. The reviewer flagged a different vacuous test (exit_code_success_is_zero
    asserting 0==0) but not this specific None-or-true pattern.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged the test with zero assertions that only checks non-panic
    via 'let _ = config'. The reviewer flagged different vacuous tests but not this
    specific zero-assertion pattern.
